# Make a Dragonkin, let him grow Hungry, photograph him, let him grow
# Starving, photograph him again.
#
# ONE ASSERTION, bd inc-i9q.3: getting hungrier must never make a character
# stronger. The sidebar prints STR and CON (src/Term.cpp), and those two
# numbers must not go UP between the two photographs.
#
# WHY A DRAGONKIN. The ordinary once-per-turn hunger tick does nothing at all
# for anybody -- that is bd inc-i9q.2, a separate defect, still open. A
# Dragonkin has Burning Hunger, which calls Creature::GetHungrier with 6
# rather than 1 and so takes the arm of that function which works. He is
# therefore the only character in the game who can be made hungry in a
# scripted session of any reasonable length. When inc-i9q.2 is fixed this
# script will still work; it will simply arrive sooner.
#
# THE COUNTS. Each Search command spends about 100 points of hunger, from a
# starting 2490. Hungry runs from 1000 down to 481 and Starving from 480 down
# to 241 (inc/Defines.h:3471-3479), so eleven Searches land inside Hungry and
# four more land inside Starving. The sidebar prints the state as a word, and
# tools/check_hunger_penalty.sh refuses to compare two photographs that are
# not one Hungry and one Starving.
#
# Menu letters move when a list changes. Run with a fixed seed;
# tools/check_hunger_penalty.sh supplies one.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
h       # Race:     [h] Lizardfolk
b       # Subrace:  [b] Dragonkin
a       # Class:    [a] Barbarian
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
c       # Alignment: [c] Neutral
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat

# Skill Manager, twice. Three RIGHTs per skill spends everything available
# without needing to know how many ranks this character has.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

# In the dungeon now, and Satiated. This first photograph is the baseline: it
# carries no hunger penalty at all, and it is what says the two below have
# moved.
@expect "Satiated"
@dump:fed

s*11    # Search, eleven times
@expect "Hungry"
@dump:hungry

s*4     # four more
@expect "Starving"
@dump:starving

@quit
